"""Create a self-contained presentation document from measured figures and notes."""
from pathlib import Path
import base64,html
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'outputs/handoff'
def figure(name):
 data=base64.b64encode((OUT/'figures'/name).read_bytes()).decode()
 return '<img alt="'+html.escape(name)+'" src="data:image/png;base64,'+data+'">'
sections=[
('Frozen-backbone decision models','<p class="lead">Applied Compute work trial<br>October 14–15, 2026</p><p>One A100 · Public labelled data · No backbone updates or LoRA</p>','Goal: explain a principled investigation, not simply maximize a repeatedly observed score. Suggested presentation length: 30 minutes.'),
('Background research','<p>Three readouts: pretrained answer tokens, a joint schema transformer, and a residual MLP.</p><p>Choice, Noul and Score share distributions over permitted alternatives.</p><p>Published adapted backbones do not establish frozen-backbone head-only quality.</p>','Explain PPLX’s 1.31M-parameter readout and Clef’s richer evidence routing. The original joint head is 128.06M on 27B. Gemma and other proposed backbones were not run.'),
('Evaluation contract','<p class="lead">11 suites · 2,111 fixed decisions</p><p>200 per suite; all 111 public-hard JevBench examples.<br>BBH subtask macro first; then equal suite weights. Misses count as wrong.</p><p>Independent public-source training/dev/calibration; all benchmark tasks excluded.</p>','Name the preprocessing choices: financial all-agree, fine-grained Circa, GPT-4o JudgeBench cohort, English Belebele, binary MC2 TruthfulQA. These are not verified vendor subsets.'),
('Completed recipes',figure('completed-recipes.png'),'Historical comparisons change multiple factors. Best completed inference is 79.49%; best completed trained head is 68.41%. Do not claim cross-seed robustness or a Jev win.'),
('Original joint head','<p class="lead">2 routing layers + 4 joint field layers</p><p>Width 1,024 · 16 attention heads · FFN 4,096 · GELU</p><p>Options cross-attend to evidence; fields interact; lexical prior plus gated residual scoring.</p><p>Frozen BF16 backbone; FP32 trainable head with BF16 autocast.</p>','Describe state/question/option spans and the final-token global vector. The 27B random head has 128,056,324 parameters; 9B has 121,762,820. No independent confidence network.'),
('E1: learning and collapse',figure('learning-and-collapse.png'),'Dev accuracy rises 32.49→66.93%. Gold balance does not explain the JudgeBench minority collapse or sentiment positive bias. Schema layout and semantic binding motivated follow-ups.'),
('E2 and E3','<p>Normalize training requests toward benchmark-shaped options.</p><p>Medium head: width 512, one routing layer, two field layers, eight attention heads.</p><p>v2: 2,553 records → v3: 7,928 records.</p><p class="lead">60.19% → 59.85%</p>','Original/Medium/Small dev scores: 73.66/73.28/68.70%. Architecture and optimizer jointly change in the original-versus-Medium comparison. More data did not establish better transfer.'),
('Autoresearch: larger backbone and runtime','<p>Frozen 9B → frozen 27B; Medium head retained.</p><p>Dev-accuracy selection replaced historical NLL selection.</p><p>Optimized kernels: approximately 1.56× warm backbone throughput, but strict numerical equivalence failed.</p>','Separate E4 fallback 60.93 from E4 optimized 61.26. Cache identity includes actual numerical runtime. Record cold compilation cost and why cached head training does not benefit from faster backbone kernels.'),
('Autoresearch: partial bidirectionality','<p class="lead">61.26% → 68.41%</p><p>Remove causality in full-attention blocks only.</p><p>Recurrent/convolution paths remain causal. Padding isolation and frozen weights are checked.</p>','Same optimized numerical regime, v3 partitions and recipe. Separate feature extraction is required. The observed +7.15 pp is single-seed and does not establish a universal improvement.'),
('Different tasks respond differently',figure('task-transfer.png'),'E5 improves finance and judging but worsens Circa and RAGTruth. A composite alone hides failure mechanisms. Discuss the native readout’s broader transfer.'),
('Autoresearch: repeatability','<p>Same seed, weights and batch windows still produced divergent fused-attention training.</p><p>Math attention matched the 32-update fixture, followed by full matched controls.</p><p>Preserve both divergent outcomes before attributing source effects.</p>','Automatic backward controls reached 58.60 and 60.85 with no source intervention. The short math fixture runs at 0.844× throughput; do not mistake conditional paired intervals for training uncertainty.'),
('Autoresearch: source additions',figure('source-additions.png'),'Each condition adds 250 native-labelled examples with equal update counts. MASSIVE passes screening but needs new-seed confirmation. RuleTaker semantic repair was a motivated negative result.'),
('Pretrained answer semantics','<p class="lead">Native 77.14% → native + reverse 79.49%</p><p>Use existing answer-letter output weights.<br>Align and average two option-order probability vectors.<br>Fit one temperature on nonbenchmark calibration.</p>','No head or backbone updates. Native and pooled prompts/readouts differ from the joint-head recipe, so this is not an isolated causal estimate of head training. Pooled T=0.9887233144498362.'),
('Pending and unscored work','<p>Bounded thinking: dev gate passed; no sealed complete benchmark result in the audited ledger.</p><p>Residual MLP: 5.52M parameters, fixed versus per-epoch shuffled option order; active.</p><p>Prepared-only controls remain explicitly unscored.</p>','W&B finished status is not proof of a completed test. Do not turn partial logits into a score. Active jobs were not changed for cleanup.'),
('Reproduction and artifacts','<p>W&B: authoritative experiment tracker.</p><p>Git: source, narrative, configs, manifests and compact traces.</p><p>Modal: accepted checkpoints, datasets and retained saved states.</p><p>One accepted checkpoint reference per run; others remain reachable.</p>','Show outputs/handoff/run-index.json and the accepted-model manifest. Distinguish a protocol digest from a weight-file checksum. Point to reproduction commands and explicit model/data pins.'),
('What we learned','<p>Preserve strong pretrained readout semantics as an early control.</p><p>Test numerical repeatability before interpreting small data effects.</p><p>Inspect prediction distributions, not only aggregate accuracy.</p><p>Best inference recipe and best trained head are separate deliverables.</p>','Conclude with limitations: reused exploratory panel, mostly single seed, no vendor-subset reproduction, no Jev superiority. Full experiment catalog and all negative/prepared results are in the report and ledger.')]
style='''body{margin:0;background:#edf0f3;color:#172132;font:22px/1.45 system-ui,sans-serif}section{box-sizing:border-box;max-width:1250px;margin:30px auto;padding:48px 64px;background:white;min-height:700px;break-after:page}h1{font-size:42px;font-weight:650;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 30px}p{max-width:1040px;margin:20px 0}.lead{font-size:38px;color:#197a6b}img{width:100%;height:auto;max-height:530px;object-fit:contain}details{margin-top:35px;font-size:16px;color:#4b5668;border-top:1px solid #ddd;padding-top:14px}footer{font-size:12px;color:#667085;margin-top:24px}a{color:#185a8c}@media print{body{background:white;font-size:18px}section{margin:0;max-width:none;min-height:0;padding:14mm;height:180mm}details{display:none}img{max-height:130mm}h1{font-size:30px}.lead{font-size:30px}@page{size:A4 landscape;margin:0}}'''
body=[]
for i,(title,content,notes) in enumerate(sections,1):body.append(f'<section><h1>{html.escape(title)}</h1>{content}<details><summary>Presenter notes</summary><p>{html.escape(notes)}</p></details><footer>{i}/{len(sections)} · Source: <a href="research-report.md">research report</a> and <a href="../autoresearch/overnight-benchmark-scores.csv">verified ledger</a> · exploratory fixed-panel results</footer></section>')
(OUT/'presentation.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Frozen-backbone decision models</title><style>'+style+'</style><body>'+''.join(body)+'</body></html>')
outline=['# Presentation notes','', 'Approximately 30 minutes; expand the notes in the self-contained HTML document.','']
for title,content,notes in sections:outline.extend(['## '+title,'',notes,''])
(ROOT/'docs/presentation-notes.md').write_text('\n'.join(outline))
print('Created',len(sections),'presentation sections with embedded figures')

# Keep downloadable Markdown links correct outside docs/.
import re,os
for name in ['research-report.md','reproduce-handoff.md','presentation-notes.md']:
 source=ROOT/'docs'/name;destination=OUT/name
 def relocate(match):
  label,url=match.groups()
  if '://' in url or url.startswith('#'):return match.group(0)
  target=(source.parent/url).resolve()
  return '['+label+']('+os.path.relpath(target,destination.parent)+')'
 destination.write_text(re.sub(r'\[([^\]]+)\]\(([^)]+)\)',relocate,source.read_text()))
